   "title": "Now you try",
   "prompt": "How many **hydrogen atoms** are in the displayed formula of **heptane**?",
   "answer": 16,
   "hint": "Use CₙH₂ₙ₊₂, or count: 3 H on each end carbon and 2 H on every other carbon.",
   "explain": "heptane has 7 carbons, so H = 2 × 7 + 2 = 16."
  },
  {
