   "hint": "Count the carbons first: pent = 5. End carbons are CH₃.",
   "explain": "pentane has 5 carbons: CH₃CH₂CH₂CH₂CH₃."
  }
 ],
 "takeaways": [
  "**Stem** = number of carbons, **-ane** = only single bonds.",
  "Fill every free place with H so each carbon has **four** bonds.",
  "Check: H atoms = 2 × C + 2 for an alkane."
 ],
 "notes": [
  {
   "title": "Exam tip",
   "text": "Write the displayed formula first (all C–H bonds drawn), then the condensed formula. Marks are lost for a carbon with only three bonds."
  }
 ]
